{"assessments": [{"claim": "H20", "status": "accept", "investigation": "closed", "evidence": ["R71", "R75"]}, {"claim": "H7", "status": "reject", "investigation": "closed", "evidence": ["R7", "R76"]}, {"claim": "H84", "status": "reject", "investigation": "closed", "evidence": ["R59", "R102"]}, {"claim": "H94", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H95", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H96", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H97", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H98", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H99", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H135", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}], "narrative": "The new validation deadlines confirm and extend the existing conclusions. H20 is the central feature_037 claim in the registered negative direction: a signed validation estimate of +0.796, interval [0.703, 0.889], means that feature_037=1 is lower by about 0.80 composite dependency-score units, i.e. stronger dependency, than feature_037=0. Even after validation multiplicity adjustment, the lower bound is far above the 0.15 threshold and agrees with discovery (+0.804 [0.742, 0.867]). I therefore reaffirm H20 as a strongly supported dataset-specific association and close it. H7 tests a feature_007-by-feature_038 interaction in the registered negative direction; signed discovery -0.026 and independent validation -0.039, validation interval [-0.213, 0.134], are near null and cross zero. Validation provides no evidence of a scientifically meaningful positive signed interaction. I reaffirm reject and close. H84 tests feature_052 level_002 versus level_003; signed discovery +0.057 crosses null and validation is essentially zero (-0.00025, [-0.229, 0.228]). Validation reinforces no meaningful difference; reject and close. No accepted claim changes result from these deadline responses.

The strongest scientific synthesis remains three large, independently supported, noncausal associations in this dataset: feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 (weaker composite dependency; H13, +0.829 discovery and +0.821 validation with lower validation bound 0.739), feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 (stronger composite dependency; H20 above), and feature_002=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 (weaker dependency; H114, +0.810 discovery and +0.846 validation with lower validation bound 0.755). Crucially, these are not simply marginal proxies for one another: each remains strongly associated within feasible conditional strata after conditioning on the other two predictors, while all exact pairwise interaction estimates among these three predictors are small, null-crossing, and not credibly above threshold. The best supported joint interpretation is therefore an approximately additive structure of persistent associations, though exact interaction effects cannot be proven to be zero because confidence intervals include modest values.

The negative evidence is also substantial. Broad screens of many binary/categorical predictors, research signatures, research markers, and context interactions repeatedly produce effects near null, including the now validated H7 and H84 results. Remaining uncertainty includes whether rare nominal levels (deferred H94-H99) or untested broad predictors hide a large association, whether the three large predictor labels share a latent data-generation structure, and whether the associations persist or attenuate in short log-progression-free survival and age extremes. Clinical context is already supported for feature_010 and for feature_037 in long PFS, but short-PFS context tests remain active. All conclusions are dataset-specific Welch associations; conditioning can induce confounding or collider-like artifacts, predictor meanings are opaque, and no causal mechanism or external generalizability can be claimed. The most informative next analysis is the active context-persistence set H144-H150. If feature_037 and feature_002 remain far above threshold in short-PFS and age-extreme strata, the conclusion becomes context-persistent additive associations. If a context contrast collapses below 0.15 or reverses, that would be a new discovery worthy of targeted validation and would materially change the interpretation. Rare-level claims remain deferred behind these higher-value context tests.", "research_notes": "Validated response deadlines reaffirmed: H20 accept (feature_037=1 stronger dependency, validation +0.796 [0.703,0.889]); H7 reject; H84 reject. Central accepted evidence: H13 feature_010=1 higher outcome_001, H20 feature_037=1 lower outcome_001, H114 feature_002=1 higher outcome_001. Exact pairwise interactions among the three are near null; conditional main effects persist far above threshold. Interpretation: approximately additive dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable. Next prioritize active H144-H150 short-PFS and age-extreme contrasts for feature_037/feature_002; follow only a large context-specific reversal/collapse. Defer rare H94-H99 and redundant H135 behind context tests."}
